--TEST--
`Iterator<T>` has `advance()` and `current()` and nothing else, so a `$k =>` binding over one is a compile error — ADR 0053 § 1
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Steps {
    public static function upto(int $n): Iterator<int> {
        int $i = 0;
        while ($i < $n) {
            yield $i;
            $i = $i + 1;
        }
    }
}

foreach (Steps::upto(3) as string $k => int $v) {
    echo $k, "=", $v, ";";
}
echo "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0444]: an `Iterable`/`Iterator` subject has no key to bind
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
